<article class="env-lemma" id="0AII">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AII">Lemma <span data-tag="0AII">87.10.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an affine formal algebraic space over $S$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
there exists a system $X_1 \to X_2 \to X_3 \to \ldots $ of thickenings of affine schemes over $S$ such that $X = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits X_ n$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there exists a choice $X = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits X_\lambda $ as in Definition <a href="/tag/0AI7" data-tag="0AI7">87.9.1</a> such that $\Lambda $ is countable. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the observation that a countable directed set has a cofinal subset isomorphic to $(\mathbf{N}, \geq )$. See proof of Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0597" data-tag="0597">10.86.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>